  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 101 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nHigh pressure will slowly move across the area today and tonight\nwith light winds and a weak lake breeze expected this afternoon.\nHigh temps will reach the upper 40s to around 50. The light\nwinds may allow for some patchy/shallow fog to develop late\ntonight into early Monday morning, mainly for areas along and\nsouth of I-80 and have added patchy fog mention for this time\nperiod with this forecast. The high pressure will move east on\nMonday with southwest winds expected through Thursday with high\ntemps slowly warming a few degrees each day with highs possibly\ntagging 60 Wednesday and Thursday and then high temps possibly\ninto the lower/mid 60s Friday and Saturday. A weak cold front\nmay move across the area Thursday bringing a low chance for a\nfew showers and then a possibly stronger cold front may move\nacross the region next weekend, bringing another chance for\nshowers as well as cooler but still seasonable temps back to \nthe region. cms",
